    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3230" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ā^prīnus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		aper, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the wild boar</i>:
			viscus, Lucil. ap. <i><span class="en">Charis. p. 63</span></i> P.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pulmo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					28, 16, 62, § 222</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vesica,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					28, 15, 60, § 215</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fel,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					28, 16, 62, § 221</span></i>
			.—As a secondary form, <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab.
				69</span></i>, has twice <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ā^prīnĕus</span></b> , a,
			um, if the reading is correct.</div>
